(x + a)^2 &= 2 \quad \Longrightarrow \\
x + a &= \pm \sqrt{2}.
\end{align*}
This gives us $x = a - \sqrt{2}$ and $x = a + \sqrt{2}.$

From the equation $y^2 = 8x,$ we get
\begin{align*}
(a + bx)^2 &= 8(a - \sqrt{2}) \\
