(a + \sqrt{2})^2 &= 8a + 8\sqrt{2}.
\end{align*}From $x = a - \sqrt{2},$ we get
\begin{align*}
(a - \sqrt{2})^2 &= 8a - 8\sqrt{2}.
\end{align*}
